{
  "__comment": "Grafana dashboard JSON for the WAT-anchor pipeline per-anchor latency histograms (Sprint Tag-12 mini-welle Per-Anchor-Latency-Histograms, Noa Bergstroem / SRE). Consumes Prometheus histogram + pre-computed percentile gauges produced by scripts/wat-anchor-pipeline-observability.py --format prom (Tag-12 extension of PR #134). Schema version targets Grafana 10.x (schemaVersion >= 38). One panel per pipeline stage (enqueue_to_pre_ots, ots_call, post_ots_commit, wat_write); each panel plots p50/p95/p99 lines side-by-side. Operational, not Vanity: every panel answers SLO-2 (anchor-latency-p99) for its stage. ADR-0064 Phase-2-operations-reife Folgeartefakt.",
  "title": "Wakir WAT-Anchor — Per-Anchor Latency Histograms",
  "uid": "wakir-wat-anchor-latency-histograms",
  "tags": ["wakir", "wat-anchor", "sre", "latency", "phase-2", "slo-2"],
  "schemaVersion": 38,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "Stage SLO-2 burn (p99 > 1s)",
        "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prom"},
        "enable": true,
        "iconColor": "red",
        "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p99_seconds > 1.0"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Stage: enqueue_to_pre_ots",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "enqueue_to_pre_ots — p50 / p95 / p99 over time",
      "description": "Latency from anchor-enqueue to the pre-OTS-call setup. Healthy baseline: p99 < 50ms; sustained > 100ms indicates contention on the enqueue path (NATS-KV writes, lock acquisition, or pre-OTS receipt allocation). SLO-2 reference: this stage should never dominate the end-to-end anchor latency.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 1},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p50_seconds{stage=\"enqueue_to_pre_ots\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p95_seconds{stage=\"enqueue_to_pre_ots\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p99_seconds{stage=\"enqueue_to_pre_ots\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 0.05},
              {"color": "red", "value": 0.1}
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 200,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Stage: ots_call",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 10},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "ots_call — p50 / p95 / p99 over time",
      "description": "Latency of the OpenTimestamps calendar HTTP call. This is the dominant stage by design — OTS calendars are external services with network-attached latency. Healthy baseline: p50 < 500ms, p95 < 2s, p99 < 5s. Sustained p99 > 10s should fire SLO-2-burn alerts; calendar HTTP timeouts manifest here first.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 11},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p50_seconds{stage=\"ots_call\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p95_seconds{stage=\"ots_call\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p99_seconds{stage=\"ots_call\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 2.0},
              {"color": "red", "value": 5.0}
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 300,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Stage: post_ots_commit",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 20},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "post_ots_commit — p50 / p95 / p99 over time",
      "description": "Latency from OTS-call return to the commit of the receipt to local storage. This is filesystem-bound work (write .ots file, update receipt-DB index). Healthy baseline: p99 < 100ms. Sustained > 250ms indicates disk I/O pressure or a receipt-DB lock-contention regression.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 21},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p50_seconds{stage=\"post_ots_commit\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p95_seconds{stage=\"post_ots_commit\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p99_seconds{stage=\"post_ots_commit\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 0.1},
              {"color": "red", "value": 0.25}
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 400,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Stage: wat_write",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 30},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "wat_write — p50 / p95 / p99 over time",
      "description": "Latency to append the verified anchor to the WAT Merkle log. Local filesystem + Merkle-recomputation work. Healthy baseline: p99 < 50ms. Sustained > 100ms indicates the WAT log is growing past a regime where the Merkle-build cost is amortized cheaply; consider a rotation cycle.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 31},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p50_seconds{stage=\"wat_write\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p95_seconds{stage=\"wat_write\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_stage_latency_p99_seconds{stage=\"wat_write\"}",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 0.05},
              {"color": "red", "value": 0.1}
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 500,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Observability context",
      "gridPos": {"h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 40},
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Window size (anchors)",
      "description": "Number of parseable latency observations the most recent script run aggregated. If this stays at zero the latency-JSONL producer (WAT-core) is not emitting; check the producer side before reading the percentile panels.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 41},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "wat_anchor_latency_window_size",
          "legendFormat": "window",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "red", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 1},
              {"color": "green", "value": 10}
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Last scrape (age)",
      "description": "Seconds since the latency-histogram script last wrote the textfile. If this grows past the systemd-timer cadence the script is failing; check journalctl --user.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 41},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "time() - wat_anchor_latency_scrape_timestamp_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "age",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "orange", "value": 900},
              {"color": "red", "value": 1800}
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
